# @epistemologic/property/tool_species_stagefreight_witnessed —
# RED property landing for StageFreight Delivery Arc 1 (Mara this
# tick). Cross-species declarative property naming what EVERY
# @tool species minted this tick (@tool/go + @tool/docker + @tool/
# gitlab_ci) AND the sibling @cascade/code/rust/go species MUST
# satisfy at substrate-decl altitude BEFORE Reed empirical firing
# ticks discharge.
#
# === Position in bilateral pattern #53 ===
#
# THIS shard is the DECLARATIVE HALF of bilateral pattern #53's
# NINTH instance (Mara-counted-from-brief; Pack-altitude
# verification deferred). Prior instances at
# `shards/epistemologic/property/`:
#   1. keyword_matches_depth
#   2. gate_matches_diff_closure
#   3. syntax_substrate_native / angle_to_paren
#   4. restart_intensity_well_formed
#   5. cold_compile_within_tolerance
#   6. dark_count_monotone
#   7. docblock_coherent / grounded / no_extraction_pattern
#   8. ouroboros_monotone + verdict_is_content_addressed
#
# Ninth instance (THIS): tool_species_stagefreight_witnessed at
# @tool species altitude. The property predicates over a landed
# @tool species (identified by tool_id variant tag) and asserts
# a composed FIVE-conjunct at species altitude:
#
#   tool_species_stagefreight_witnessed(species: tool_id, p) ⇔
#       tool_invocation_admissible_inherited(species, p)
#     ∧ discharge_through_io(species, p)
#     ∧ fate_biased_execute(species, p)
#     ∧ tool_invocation_signed_at_alex_root(species, p)
#     ∧ tool_result_witnessed_content_addressed(species, p)
#
# The operational half (the fracture body that emits a widen/
# raise/surface morphism when any conjunct fails) is DEFERRED to
# Reed's Arc 3 territory per StageFreight spec §7.3 Tick 11-15;
# the FRACTURE lives at `@kintsugi/fracture/tool_species_
# stagefreight_broken` (forward-promised). The paired-fracture
# pattern MAY consolidate under `@kintsugi/fracture/tool_
# species_unwitnessed` if the failure modes converge.
#
# === Why RED ===
#
# All four @tool species (@tool/go + @tool/docker + @tool/gitlab_ci
# + @cascade/code/rust/go's dispatch surface) landed this tick as
# substrate-decl SHAPES. Their bodies are `\`-blocked per
# `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`. This property NAMES the
# invariants that MUST hold when the bodies discharge; empirically,
# the invariants are UNWITNESSED as of the tick this property lands.
#
# RED semantics (analytical, not runtime):
#   - The five sub-predicates below CANNOT be discharged at
#     substrate-decl altitude alone; they require @io boundary
#     dispatch (species .exec bodies discharging via @io.exec).
#   - Reed's Arc 2 (Tick 6-10) empirically fires the dispatch;
#     the transition RED → GREEN happens WHEN Reed's tick discharges
#     each species' body against a real subprocess AND the resulting
#     tool_result carries a substrate-decl'd witnessed_run + @trust
#     signature terminating at @alex root.
#   - Until then, this property serves as the FIRST-CLASS DECLARATION
#     of what "witnessed" MEANS for a @tool species minted for
#     StageFreight delivery.
#
# === The five conjuncts (why each MUST hold) ===
#
# 1. `tool_invocation_admissible_inherited` — the species' composed
#    bilateral `<species>_invocation_well_formed` MUST include the
#    family-root `tool_invocation_admissible` requires-clause.
#    Verified at substrate-decl altitude: grep the species shard for
#    `requires tool_invocation_admissible(invocation, invocation, p)`.
#    Present in @tool/go + @tool/docker + @tool/gitlab_ci this tick.
#    Present in @tool/cargo + @tool/git + @tool/nix from earlier this
#    session. INVARIANT: no @tool species may compose without
#    inheriting the family-root admissibility gate.
#
# 2. `discharge_through_io` — the species' exec action MUST
#    dispatch through @io.<action> at mechanism altitude; MUST NOT
#    author its own subprocess spawn primitive. Per HARD RULE
#    `feedback_no_rust_extension_shortcut` + Alex 2026-07-16
#    8th-repetition `feedback_detector_inadequacy_answer_is_never_
#    rust`. Verified at substrate-decl altitude via docblock text
#    ("dispatches ─▶ @io.exec" pattern in each species). Reed
#    empirical verification: no `.rs` extension file authored under
#    `shards/**` this tick for these species (grep should return
#    empty; species compose over @io by construction).
#
# 3. `fate_biased_execute` — the species' exec dispatch MUST be
#    selectable by Fate at @roomba walker altitude per closure §7.3
#    empirical firing surface 4. `@roomba.walk(stagefreight.spec)`
#    emits a sequence of `@tool(X, args)` invocations; Fate biases
#    the dispatch order per @fate.bias(target). The invariant:
#    every species minted for StageFreight delivery MUST be
#    addressable via `tool_id` variant tag at Fate altitude. Verified
#    at substrate-decl altitude: species tool_id present in @tool
#    family-root's tool_id closed variant (shards/tool.mirror lines
#    185-199). go + docker + gitlab_ci ALL PRESENT.
#
# 4. `tool_invocation_signed_at_alex_root` — every discharged
#    tool_invocation MUST carry a signature field resolvable through
#    the @trust chain terminating at @alex root. THIS conjunct is
#    the LOAD-BEARING PR-delivery gate per StageFreight spec §6 PR
#    body structure ("Signed-off-by: mirror <peer@spectral.engineer>
#    via @trust chain rooted at @alex"). Substrate-decl'd altitude:
#    tool_invocation.signature field present (shards/tool.mirror
#    :220). Reed empirical verification: @trust family-root lands as
#    Mara territory NEXT tick (per closure §12.2); until then, the
#    signature field is `ref` and this conjunct is DEFERRED-RED per
#    forward-promise composition.
#
# 5. `tool_result_witnessed_content_addressed` — every tool_result
#    MUST carry a witness field whose OID round-trips through
#    @mirror/store per @kintsugi/roomba's content-addressed run-
#    provenance discipline. Composes with family-root's
#    `tool_result_witnessed` bilateral (shards/tool.mirror :348).
#    Substrate-decl'd altitude: witness field present in tool_result
#    (shards/tool.mirror :241). Reed empirical verification: first
#    @tool/go(test, [./...]) dispatch against StageFreight repo MUST
#    return a tool_result whose witness OID resolves via `mirror
#    recall <oid>` (per @mirror/recall action, LANDED).
#
# === Rice-safety ===
#
# Per emergent-supervision §5.4: the substrate cannot ask "will
# this species dispatch always terminate?" (Rice forbids it). This
# property asks the DECIDABLE questions at substrate-decl altitude:
#
#   - Is the family-root admissibility requires-clause present in
#     the species shard? (Grep-decidable at substrate-decl altitude.)
#   - Does the species dispatch through @io per docblock declaration?
#     (Grep-decidable + substrate-audit-decidable via [substrate-
#     floor:@io-boundary] marker discipline.)
#   - Is the species' tool_id present in the family-root variant?
#     (Type-checkable at substrate-decl altitude.)
#   - Is the signature field present in tool_invocation? (Type-
#     checkable.)
#   - Is the witness field present in tool_result? (Type-checkable.)
#
# All five conjuncts are DECIDABLE at substrate-decl altitude via
# structural inspection; the UNDECIDABLE question ("will Marcus's
# real StageFreight dispatch actually satisfy these?") is Reed's
# empirical territory, not this property's scope.
#
# === Composition with @tool species this tick ===
#
# Verified this tick at substrate-decl altitude:
#
# | Species          | conjunct 1 | conjunct 2 | conjunct 3 | conjunct 4 | conjunct 5 |
# |------------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|------------|
# | @tool/cargo      | present    | present    | tool_id in variant | DEFERRED (Mara @trust next tick) | present via tool_result |
# | @tool/git        | present    | present    | tool_id in variant | DEFERRED                          | present                 |
# | @tool/nix        | present    | present    | tool_id in variant | DEFERRED                          | present                 |
# | @tool/go         | present    | present    | tool_id in variant | DEFERRED                          | present                 |
# | @tool/docker     | present    | present    | tool_id in variant | DEFERRED                          | present                 |
# | @tool/gitlab_ci  | present    | present    | tool_id in variant | DEFERRED                          | present                 |
#
# Six species; conjunct 4 uniformly DEFERRED pending @trust family-
# root landing next Mara tick. Reed's Arc 3 Tick 14 closes conjunct
# 4 empirically.
#
# @cascade/code/rust/go composes ADJACENT to this property (not IN
# it, since @cascade species are NOT @tool species — different
# family-root). @cascade/code/rust/go composition with @tool/go is
# what StageFreight spec §5 composition graph names: cascade emits
# Go source; @tool/go invokes the go binary against it. The @cascade
# species carries its own composed bilateral
# `rust_go_cascade_well_formed` at species-decl altitude; the two
# families compose at the empirical-firing altitude.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Floyd-Hoare precondition   Floyd 1967 + Hoare 1969. This property
#                              IS a Hoare precondition over the
#                              @tool species discharge boundary; the
#                              postcondition is the tool_result +
#                              witnessed_run + @trust-signature.
#   TDD RED / GREEN cycle     Beck 2002 *Test-Driven Development by
#                              Example*. RED = property named before
#                              body discharges; GREEN = body discharges
#                              such that property holds. Reed's
#                              [substrate-floor:@io-boundary] marker
#                              gates the RED → GREEN transition per
#                              Pack discipline.
#   Bilateral pattern #53      Reed + Mara 2026-06-10 through 2026-
#                              07-03; this is the ninth instance of
#                              the property/fracture bilateral pair
#                              at cross-species altitude.
#
# === Substrate gaps surfaced honestly ===
#
# - Conjunct 4 (@trust chain signature) is DEFERRED-RED for all six
#   @tool species until Mara's next-tick @trust family-root lands.
#   This is architecturally load-bearing: the substrate cannot
#   substrate-decl "signed by @trust chain" without the @trust
#   family-root existing. Cascade-tick discipline: this property
#   forward-promises the conjunct 4 resolution.
#
# - The Mara-counted-from-brief "ninth instance" count MAY drift
#   from Pack-altitude counting; Seam Phase D audit is authoritative.
#
# - The composed-bilateral shape here has FIVE conjuncts vs prior
#   instances' 3-4. This is honest: cross-species composition at
#   substrate-decl altitude admits more sub-predicates because the
#   invariant surface is wider (family-root admissibility + @io
#   discharge + Fate addressability + @trust signing + witness
#   content-addressing).
#
# - The property fires at DECLARATION time (Mara this tick); the
#   paired fracture fires at REALISATION time (Reed Arc 3 Tick 11-15
#   when species bodies discharge against Marcus's StageFreight
#   repo). Timing separation per emergent-supervision §5.5 H4.
#
# Spec context: `docs/specs/2026-07-18-stagefreight-delivery.md`
#               §3 + §4.2 + §7.1 Tick 5 (Mara canonical spec; THIS
#               property is the Tick 5 discharge — RED property
#               tests naming what each new species MUST satisfy);
#               `docs/specs/2026-07-18-the-compiler-in-one-sentence.
#               md` §3.4 + §7.3 empirical firing surface 4 (the
#               fate-biased-execute conjunct source);
#               `shards/tool.mirror` (family-root; tool_id variant
#               at :185; tool_invocation.signature at :220;
#               tool_result.witness at :241; the substrate-decl'd
#               field surface conjuncts 3-5 predicate over).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]
#                       (#53; ninth instance),
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]
#                       (@epistemologic = form-side family root;
#                       this property sits form-side; the paired
#                       fracture at @kintsugi will sit process-side),
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (the
#                       property's decidability rests on landed
#                       tool_id + tool_invocation + tool_result
#                       carriers at @tool family-root),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (conjuncts predicate
#                       over typed species carriers, not stringly-
#                       compared species names),
#                      [[feedback-no-rust-extension-shortcut]]
#                       (conjunct 2 is the direct grep-audit of THIS
#                       HARD RULE at cross-species altitude — every
#                       @tool species discharges through @io; NO Rust
#                       extension authorship this tick),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (grep 2026-07-18 this tick confirmed no
#                       `tool_species_stagefreight` precedent; the
#                       ninth-instance naming follows the eight prior
#                       instances' substrate-decl vocabulary).
# Related shards: shards/tool.mirror (family-root; conjuncts 3-5
#                  predicate over carriers landed here),
#                 shards/tool/cargo.mirror + shards/tool/git.mirror +
#                 shards/tool/nix.mirror (three species from earlier
#                  in this session; all six species this property
#                  ranges over),
#                 shards/tool/go.mirror + shards/tool/docker.mirror +
#                 shards/tool/gitlab_ci.mirror (three species minted
#                  this tick; StageFreight-delivery-specific range),
#                 shards/cascade/code/rust/go.mirror (adjacent
#                  species; @cascade family-root NOT @tool; composes
#                  at empirical-firing altitude per StageFreight
#                  spec §5 composition graph),
#                 shards/epistemologic/property/restart_intensity_
#                  well_formed.mirror (sibling in @epistemologic/
#                  property; fourth instance whose docblock shape
#                  THIS property mirrors — same conjunct discipline,
#                  same Rice-safety framing, same RED discipline
#                  before empirical discharge),
#                 shards/epistemologic/property/verdict_is_content_
#                  addressed.mirror (sibling; conjunct 5 composes
#                  over this sibling's content-addressed-verdict
#                  discipline at witness altitude).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/property/tool_species_stagefreight_
# witnessed.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/property/tool_species_stagefreight_witnessed`
# per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/floyd-hoare-1969
source @arxiv/testing/beck-2002-tdd

prism @epistemologic/property/tool_species_stagefreight_witnessed {
  focus tool_species_witness
  project tool_species_witness
  split tool_species_witness
  shift tool_species_witness
  settle tool_species_witness
}

# ============================================================
# §2 Sub-predicates (the five conjuncts)
# ============================================================

# === tool_invocation_admissible_inherited ===
#
# Verdict that the species' composed bilateral
# `<species>_invocation_well_formed` includes the family-root
# `tool_invocation_admissible` requires-clause.
#
# Splinter-pole: `requires tool_invocation_admissible(invocation,
# invocation, p)` clause present in species' composed bilateral.
# Narcissus-pole: species composes without inheriting family-root
# admissibility gate; @tool/X.<action>_well_formed does not
# require the family-root check → species-level admissibility
# claim MAY drift from family-root discipline.
tool_invocation_admissible_inherited(species: tool_id, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# === discharge_through_io ===
#
# Verdict that the species' exec action dispatches through @io.
# <action> at mechanism altitude and does NOT author its own
# subprocess spawn primitive.
#
# Splinter-pole: species docblock declares "dispatches ─▶ @io.
# <action>" composition direction; no `.rs` extension file authored
# under `shards/**` for this species this tick; [substrate-floor:
# @io-boundary] marker discipline honored.
# Narcissus-pole: species authors its own subprocess spawn;
# species extends Rust extension directly for dispatch; HARD RULE
# `feedback_no_rust_extension_shortcut` violated.
discharge_through_io(species: tool_id, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# === fate_biased_execute ===
#
# Verdict that the species' exec dispatch is selectable by Fate at
# @roomba walker altitude — the species' `tool_id` variant tag IS
# present in @tool family-root's tool_id closed variant enumeration.
#
# Splinter-pole: species' tool_id tag present in `shards/tool.
# mirror` :185-199 tool_id variant enumeration; @roomba can emit
# `@tool(<tag>, args)` for this species; Fate can bias dispatch
# ordering per closure §7.3 empirical firing surface 4.
# Narcissus-pole: species tool_id absent from family-root variant
# enumeration → @roomba cannot dispatch → Fate cannot bias →
# empirical firing surface 4 broken at this species.
fate_biased_execute(species: tool_id, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# === tool_invocation_signed_at_alex_root ===
#
# Verdict that every discharged tool_invocation carries a
# signature field resolvable through the @trust chain terminating
# at @alex root.
#
# Splinter-pole: tool_invocation.signature field present at family-
# root altitude (SUBSTRATE-DECL'd); species inherit the field; when
# @trust family-root lands (Mara next tick), the signature field
# resolves through the chain; @alex root terminates the chain per
# StageFreight spec §6 PR delivery structure.
# Narcissus-pole: signature field missing; @trust chain absent;
# @alex root not terminating; PR delivery cannot be signed per
# StageFreight commitment to Marcus.
#
# NOTE: this conjunct is DEFERRED-RED until @trust family-root
# lands next Mara tick. The signature FIELD is present at family-
# root altitude this tick; the CHAIN discharge is forward-promised.
tool_invocation_signed_at_alex_root(species: tool_id, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# === tool_result_witnessed_content_addressed ===
#
# Verdict that every tool_result carries a witness field whose OID
# round-trips through @mirror/store per @kintsugi/roomba's content-
# addressed run-provenance discipline.
#
# Splinter-pole: tool_result.witness field present at family-root
# altitude; witness carries a witnessed_run per @kintsugi/roomba;
# witness OID resolves via `mirror recall <oid>`; composes with
# family-root's `tool_result_witnessed` bilateral (shards/tool.
# mirror :348).
# Narcissus-pole: witness field is bare `ref` with no provenance
# chain; witness OID does not round-trip through @mirror/store;
# tool_result claimed without witness backing.
tool_result_witnessed_content_addressed(species: tool_id, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# ============================================================
# §3 The composed property
# ============================================================

# === witnessed composed bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed predicate. Returns verdict that the
# @tool species IS StageFreight-witnessed — all five sub-conjuncts
# hold at substrate-decl altitude (with conjunct 4 admissible-as-
# deferred until @trust family-root lands).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the @kintsugi loop's
# active_pass reads this predicate during Reed's Arc 3 empirical
# firing tick. The operational half (the fracture body that emits
# a widen/raise/surface morphism when this predicate fails) is
# forward-promised to Reed's Arc 3 territory.
#
# Verdict semantics:
#   success            — all five conjuncts hold (or conjunct 4
#                        admissibly-deferred per @trust forward-
#                        promise); species is StageFreight-witnessed;
#                        empirical firing may proceed.
#   failure(opacity_map)
#                      — at least one conjunct fails; the opacity_map
#                        names the offending conjunct (and, for
#                        conjunct 2, the specific `.rs` extension
#                        file that violated the HARD RULE). The
#                        paired fracture body reads one opacity at
#                        a time; conjunct-2 failures ROLL BACK to
#                        the @tool species altitude and refuse the
#                        landing per Seam Phase D audit discipline.
bilateral tool_species_stagefreight_witnessed {
  sentinel "property=tool-species-admissible-io-fate-signed-witnessed"
  arity 5
}
tool_species_stagefreight_witnessed(species: tool_id, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict
requires tool_invocation_admissible_inherited(species, p)
requires discharge_through_io(species, p)
requires fate_biased_execute(species, p)
requires tool_result_witnessed_content_addressed(species, p)
{ \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 Forward-promised
# ============================================================
#
# 1. Conjunct 4 (`tool_invocation_signed_at_alex_root`) requires-
#    clause promotion — currently omitted from the composed
#    predicate's requires-list because @trust family-root has not
#    landed. NEXT MARA TICK: @trust lands; the requires-clause
#    inserts here without shape change.
# 2. Operational fracture pair — `@kintsugi/fracture/tool_species_
#    stagefreight_broken` OR `@kintsugi/fracture/tool_species_
#    unwitnessed` (naming decision at Reed Arc 3 tick). Emits
#    widen/raise/surface morphisms per compiler-error-surface §8
#    three-mode algebra when this property fails at empirical
#    firing altitude.
# 3. Sixth conjunct forward-promise — `@coherence_rises_after_
#    dispatch` — the tool_result MUST compose into a peer-graph
#    @coherence measurement whose Fiedler λ_2 rises after landing
#    (per StageFreight spec §4.2 step 6). Currently OUT of this
#    property's substrate-decl range because @coherence measurement
#    is per-invocation-sequence, not per-species. Composes at
#    higher altitude in Reed's Arc 3 Tick 13.
# 4. Cross-arc property — `tool_species_polyglot_witnessed` at
#    cross-language altitude (per StageFreight recognition candidate
#    #R-the-compiler-delivers-across-languages). Would range over
#    (species, cascade_species) pairs; forward-promised at Reed's
#    Arc 3 Tick 15 landing.

# ============================================================
# §5 Outbound declarations
# ============================================================

out @epistemologic/property/tool_species_stagefreight_witnessed
out tool_invocation_admissible_inherited
out discharge_through_io
out fate_biased_execute
out tool_invocation_signed_at_alex_root
out tool_result_witnessed_content_addressed
out tool_species_stagefreight_witnessed
